            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@justinmk Can you clarify on diverting the `[count]` case? A nonzero count already takes the synchronous C path and does not call Lua. It is `z=` without `[count]` that is problematic.\r\n\r\nI think the approach in this PR is reasonable and small enough. Once `z=` hands control to an async picker, preserving the invoking window and buffer across the cleanup and callback is (afaik) sufficient for completing that operation correctly.\r\n",
